# CareerLockin design system

Applies to marketing pages, app shell, roadmap UI, dashboard, and settings. See `docs/landing.md` for copy tone.

## Brand & tone

- Calm, confident, direct. Clarity over overload — the product sells one clear path, not hype.
- Human-first copy: avoid "AI-powered", "revolutionary", "game-changing", urgency/countdowns, fake testimonials.
- Progress tracking is optional — do not sell commitment theater; tracking is for users who want it.
- Prefer short sentences. No em-dash filler. No invented social proof or logos.

## Visual language

- Typography: Geist (`font-sans` / `--font-geist-sans`). Headings `font-semibold tracking-tight`. Body `text-muted-foreground` for secondary text.
- Color: use CSS variables from `app/globals.css` only (`background`, `foreground`, `primary`, `muted`, `border`, `card`, `success`, `chart-*`). No ad-hoc hex/rgb, purple gradients, glassmorphism, or neon accents.
- Spacing: consistent section rhythm (`py-16 sm:py-24`), container `max-w-4xl lg:max-w-5xl xl:max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6`. Prefer whitespace over cramming.
- Components: import from `@/components/ui/*` (shadcn). Do not add new UI libraries without explicit request.
- Icons: Lucide, sparingly. One icon per list row or section label is enough.
- Motion: subtle only (hover/focus). No autoplay, parallax, or scroll-jacking.

## Layout anti-patterns (AI slop)

- Do not default to hero → three equal feature cards → pricing → footer for every page.
- Avoid identical card grids when a list, timeline, or single focal preview works better.
- One primary CTA per viewport section. Secondary actions use `variant="secondary"` or text links.
- Marketing: show the product early (preview/mock) before repeating tier bullets.
- App UI: one primary action per step/screen; progressive disclosure (accordions, collapsibles) over walls of cards.

## Charts & data (Recharts)

- Library: Recharts only (see `app/(app)/dashboard/*-chart.tsx`).
- Style: `var(--chart-1)` … `var(--chart-5)` fills; `var(--muted-foreground)` axis ticks; minimal gridlines (`axisLine={false}`, `tickLine={false}`).
- Prefer bar/line for trends; avoid pie charts and 3D. Max 2 chart types per dashboard view.
- KPI cards: one number, one label, optional small trend — no rainbow stat grids.
- Empty/loading/error states required for async chart data.

## Surface-specific notes

- **Landing** (`app/page.tsx`, `components/marketing/**`): scannable sections, product preview, single pricing block, calm FAQ accordion.
- **Roadmap** (`app/(app)/roadmap/**`): phase accordions, step detail modals — match existing patterns; avoid badge soup.
- **Dashboard** (`app/(app)/dashboard/**`): insights behind Pro gate; charts stay readable in light and dark mode.
- **Onboarding**: short forms, clear progress — reduce choices per step.

## Before shipping UI changes

- Match surrounding files' patterns and naming.
- Ensure light + dark mode both look intentional (test `html.dark`).
- Run `pnpm lint` and `pnpm typecheck`.
